FUN_0000_2ccd (per-index color/attribute lookup): dynamic-ES base loss + overlapping undefined4 typing.

Reached from the mode-set finalizer FUN_0000_2c92.  asm 0x2ccd clamps al (>=0x10 -> 0); if al differs from
the cached index byte [0x15b4], it swaps it in and does a table lookup: si=al*2; es=DGROUP:0x716 (the 4th
driver template buffer, copied by the init f98b call #4); si=es:[si]; then reads 4 bytes + 2 words from
es:si into DGROUP:0x15da/0x15dc/0x15e0/0x15de (bytes) and 0x15e2/0x15e4 (words).  Ghidra dropped the
`mov es,[0x716]` load and the string-op ES base (the offset table was dereferenced as a bare host pointer
-> SIGSEGV), and typed the 2-byte-stride word targets 0x15da.. as undefined4 (overlapping).  Rebase to the
DGROUP:0x716 ES segment and use explicit 16-bit stores; [0x15b4] is a byte compare/xchg.  Asm-verified
